{"kind":"text","seq":38,"text":"My best coaster this round scored **6.67 excitement**, which is the banked score. It's a 70-piece closed circuit with a 13-tile chain lift and a steep 60° first drop. It has four inversions: three vertical loops and a corkscrew, with boosters to keep it moving, plus airtime camelback hills and brakes before the station. The test run had no crash. Intensity was 10.02, just over the ~10 guideline; excitement didn't drop because of it. Its similarity to stock designs is 0.39, under the 0.5 penalty threshold.\n\nI also tested a softer version with a slower loop booster, which brought intensity down to 9.91. Its excitement was 6.66, slightly lower, so it didn't replace the best score."}
